      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Does any span still keep the error message or stack?\nA span can carry error text in three places: the **status description**, and the `exception.message` and `exception.stacktrace` attributes of the exception event. The target is **none**: the span keeps only `exception.type` (\"conformant\") and the text goes to the error log.\n\n**Status:** database spans conform (A36); HTTP/gRPC server and client spans in Go, Python and Node.js conform too (A37, done 2026-11-19). .NET is parked (C20/C21), so the remaining bars are expected to be `dotnet` only. The numbers count **spans** in the range.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "tempo",
        "uid": "tempo"
      },
      "description": "Spans that **received** the request (api, backend). A37 target: 0, except .NET (parked).",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "noValue": "0",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green"
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 2,
